Google services the demo calls
  Gemini on Vertex AI (grammar compiler, voice shelf check, district officer's brief),
  Cloud Run, BigQuery, Google Maps Routes API, Pub/Sub (the live feed, once deploy/live.sh is run).
  Also: Gemini on Vertex AI reading photos of paper registers (anumaan/intake.py);
  Gemini-TTS on Vertex AI (gemini-2.5-flash-tts) reading the brief aloud; BigQuery AI.FORECAST
  with TimesFM 2.5 (an offline re-test, anumaan/timesfm_retest.json; the app does not call it);
  the Routes API for the Kerala replay's road times (fetched once, cached).

Real data
  anumaan/realcheck_england.json holds monthly totals per integrated care board drawn from the
  English Prescribing Dataset, NHS Business Services Authority Open Data Portal
  (https://opendata.nhsbsa.net/dataset/english-prescribing-data-epd), fetched 30 September 2026.
  Contains public sector information licensed under the Open Government Licence v3.0.
  The file lists the official shortage notices it relies on, each with its source.

  anumaan/realcheck_india.json holds district-month totals from the Health Management
  Information System (HMIS), Ministry of Health and Family Welfare, Government of India:
  Standard Reports, C2 'Data Itemwise Monthly (up to sub district)', 'All States and Districts
  Across Months', FY 2017-18 to 2019-20 (https://hmis.mohfw.gov.in).
  Source: HMIS, Ministry of Health and Family Welfare, Government of India. The portal states
  no open licence (its Terms of Use, https://hmis.mohfw.gov.in/components/public/terms.html:
  'for reference purposes only'); the same item-wise monthly reports are published on
  data.gov.in under the Government Open Data License - India (GODL-India). The files are
  headed 'Provisional Figures'; the file lists each zip's URL and sha256.

Real locations (the Kerala replay)
  anumaan/kerala_phcs.json lists 70 public Primary/Family Health Centre locations in Kerala,
  five per district, taken from OpenStreetMap through the Overpass API; their
  districts come from OpenStreetMap's district boundaries. The same 70 coordinates key the
  Kerala road times in anumaan/road_minutes.json. Map data (c) OpenStreetMap contributors,
  available under the Open Database License 1.0 (https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/,
  https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright). kerala_phcs.json and those coordinates are made
  available under the same licence. Every record the replay shows at these locations is
  synthetic, and the facilities' names are not shown.
  Road times between them: Google Maps Platform Routes API (computeRouteMatrix), fetched once and cached.

Reports the Kerala replay follows (anumaan/scenario.py; the replay's records are synthetic)
  Onmanorama, 22 September 2026, "Bureaucratic paralysis chokes medicine supplies in
  government hospitals"; Onmanorama, 29 September 2026, "Medicine stocks available at
  hospitals, shortage at KMSCL warehouses: DMOs inform health minister". Quoted briefly, with links.

Source documents for the compiled grammar (grammar/crg/compiled.json)
  The PDFs are not redistributed here; grammar/sources/urls.txt lists where each came from.
  Each rule in compiled.json cites its source file, page and a short quote.
  - Indian Council of Medical Research: Standard Treatment Workflows for acute respiratory
    infection in adults, hypertension in adults, and urinary tract infections.
  - Ministry of Health and Family Welfare: Anemia Mukt Bharat operational guidelines (2018).
  - NCDC / MoHFW: NPCDCS training module for medical officers (2017), via NHSRC.
  - National Health Systems Resource Centre: training module for community health officers
    on acute simple illnesses (2022).
  grammar/crg/tracer.json is hand-written; the compiler only uses its condition and drug names.
